 * Configuration:

  Now you are ready to configure the FPOFL for your system. Start the FPOFL
  program from Cnet, by typing FL. You should now see a menu similar to this
  one:

 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
          _______________________________________________________
          ]   Flux Point Amiga BBS Online Filelist Generator.   [
          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
    FPOFL v1.0 (C) 1994 by PMK.  -  Flux Point Amiga BBS  +45 3526 2527


     [F]  Full Filelist.
     [D]  <x> Days back.
     [C]  Since Last call.      (08 Jul 1994)
     [L]  Since last Filelist.  (30 Jun 1994)
     [T]  The Top <x> most downloaded files for each area.
     [U]  List of files that YOU have uploaded.
   * [G]  GLOBAL Filelist. (Includes EVERYTHING!!)
   * [A]  Change Access Group. (current=31  flags=4)
   * [H]  Change Active User.  (current=[1] Pmk)
   * [X]  Load FPOFL'S Config Module.
     [P]  Change compression method. (current=.LHA)
     [S]  Change/View FileList settings.

     [Q] Quit FPOFL.

     Select Option:?  .

 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Those marked with an '*' to the left of the key, is Local Mode Only Commands
  (Sysop Commands).

  Now select the '[X]  Load FPOFL's Config Module.' option, and it will load
  the Config module. An new menu will appear, similar to this one:

 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                            ________________________________
                                           |Flux Point VisualDataEditor     |
                                           |Use cursor keys; ENTER to select|
 ___________________                        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
|<<Exit             |
 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
 ___________________
|Filelister program:| PFiles:FPOFL/MBLIST/MBLister
|Filelist Header   :| S:FPOINT.hdr
|Filelist Footer   :|
 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
 ___________________                ________________________
|Filelister type   :| MBLister     |Include Invitation Only:| No
|Write usage to log:| Yes          |Include Direct/CDROM   :| No
|Include Private   :| No           |Include Unvalidated    :| No
 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  At the 'Filelister program:' prompt, you enter the name/path of the Filelist
  program, that you want to use.
  If you want a header/footer on the filelist, then fill in the name/path of
  your Header/Footer file(s) in the 'Filelist Header:' 'Filelist Footer:'
  input fields.
  Then select the type of Filelister user. Make sure you use the same as you 
  specified in the 'Filelister program:' input field. The rest should speak
  for itself!!

   NOTE: The value of the 'Include Direct/CDRom   :' option is not available
         in MBlister, so if you have selected MBlister, then this option will
         be ignored.

  Now select the EXIT button, and save the config.
 
  To make a quick test of the setup, type '?' at the prompt. you should then
  se a version list of the various program parts. If this looks OK, then you
  are ready to create your first filelist!!



 * Known Bugs:

   When using MBLister, then the '[U] List of files that YOU have uploaded.'
  option generates a top list of ALL areas a user has access to, including
  PRIVATE and UNVALIDATED FILES!!! - MBLister 2nd bug: When using fileflag '0'
  in the UDBASE, makes MBLister create a list of ALL areas, WITHOUT checking
  the access level! SO DO NOT USE FILEFLAG '0' IF YOU ARE USING MBLISTER!!!

  Also DO NOT USE FILEFLAG '31' as ARexx can't handle 32bit numbers, so if an
  area has the '31' flag set, the value parsed to the filelister, will be 
  wrong! (It should be possible to manipulate 32bit numbers by using the AREXX
  command NUMERIC DIGITS 10, but it DOESN'T!!!


